From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - return the output IV for CBC and CTR

The crypto API expects an skcipher to leave in req->iv the IV that
continues the operation in a following request. The driver never writes
req->iv, so every CBC and CTR self-test fails with "wrong output IV",
and users that chain requests get wrong results.

Set the output IV when the last chunk of a request completes:
- CBC encryption: the last ciphertext block, read back from req->dst.
- CBC decryption: the last ciphertext block. handle_skcipher_req()
  already saves it in msg_buf.iv_ctr before the request is sent, because
  an in-place request overwrites it.
- CTR: the counter in msg_buf.iv_ctr, which handle_skcipher_req()
  advances by the whole blocks sent, plus one for a partial last block.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -463,6 +463,29 @@ static int handle_skcipher_req(struct iproc_reqctx_s *rctx)
 	return -EINPROGRESS;
 }
 
+static void skcipher_set_output_iv(struct iproc_reqctx_s *rctx,
+				   struct skcipher_request *req)
+{
+	unsigned int ivsize = rctx->iv_ctr_len;
+
+	switch (rctx->ctx->cipher.mode) {
+	case CIPHER_MODE_CBC:
+		if (rctx->is_encrypt)
+			sg_copy_part_to_buf(req->dst, req->iv, ivsize,
+					    rctx->total_todo - ivsize);
+		else
+			memcpy(req->iv, rctx->msg_buf.iv_ctr, ivsize);
+		break;
+	case CIPHER_MODE_CTR:
+		if (rctx->total_todo % AES_BLOCK_SIZE)
+			add_to_ctr(rctx->msg_buf.iv_ctr, 1);
+		memcpy(req->iv, rctx->msg_buf.iv_ctr, ivsize);
+		break;
+	default:
+		break;
+	}
+}
+
 /**
  * handle_skcipher_resp() - Process a block cipher SPU response. Updates the
  * total received count for the request and updates global stats.
@@ -497,6 +520,7 @@ static void handle_skcipher_resp(struct iproc_reqctx_s *rctx)
 
 	rctx->total_received += payload_len;
 	if (rctx->total_received == rctx->total_todo) {
+		skcipher_set_output_iv(rctx, req);
 		atomic_inc(&iproc_priv.op_counts[SPU_OP_CIPHER]);
 		atomic_inc(
 		   &iproc_priv.cipher_cnt[ctx->cipher.alg][ctx->cipher.mode]);
